#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147399 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3798ec35-19ef-559f-b8f8-cb0a0a03157b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Minimum or Maximum of a Function Given Its Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae082c6-947e-5375-a9f4-aa88253e382d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "188" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ae082c6-947e-5375-a9f4-aa88253e382d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "188" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318032} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cc1a0df-9be5-533e-b00c-ee8fecf41b26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06774482-8185-522a-b0da-abe466cad0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06774482-8185-522a-b0da-abe466cad0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317591} :answer-field/id #uuid "57c75693-c5b3-5428-8192-d75e3b45beab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b0963b7-9111-575b-994d-33c581e812aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-349996" :question/problem "On a certain afternoon, the total number of people $N(t)$ visiting the city's zoo is given by the function\n\n$$\nN(t)=60+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(48-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time (in hours) since noon.  \n\nAt what time is the number of people in the zoo at a maximum, and how many people are at the zoo at that time?\n\nThe maximum number of people is\n{{field-1}}\nafter\n{{field-2}}\nhours." :question/worked-solution "To find when the number of people at the zoo is at maximum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(60+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(48-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(60)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(48-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(48-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =48-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=0$:\n\n$$\n48-3{t}^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,t=4\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=4.$ To find out how many people are in the zoo when $t=4,$ we figure out $N(4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(4) & =60+{\\int }_{0}^{4}(48-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =60+{[48x-{x}^{3}]|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =60+[(48\\cdot 4-{4}^{3})-(0)] \\\\  & =60+[192-64] \\\\  & =60+128 \\\\  & =188\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $60<188$, we conclude that the maximum number of people at the zoo is $188$, and this will happen after $4$ hours."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147399 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3798ec35-19ef-559f-b8f8-cb0a0a03157b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Minimum or Maximum of a Function Given Its Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21c10ece-c009-56c5-be8d-90e6cb75497c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The minimum is $40$ participants  after $4$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330238} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7ffa2f-9e56-5efe-97c7-d12ccab36064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The minimum is $32$ participants  after $0$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330645} {:answer/id #uuid "522f2b59-ef0a-5794-8023-90cf98db584b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The minimum is $8$ participants  after $4$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330698} {:answer/id #uuid "d7eb419f-421f-54a3-b0b8-0034e420363a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The minimum is $40$ participants  after $0$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331864} {:answer/id #uuid "f18e8e04-35b4-55b7-86fa-527938e47ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The minimum is $32$ participants  after $4$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "522f2b59-ef0a-5794-8023-90cf98db584b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The minimum is $8$ participants  after $4$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330698} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9450f60-3299-5ac4-9582-ce92545753e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28fcc32f-48c3-5813-8388-8eda5e584ffe" :question/math-academy-id "q-62834" :question/problem "The total number of participants $S(t)$ registered for an online conference after $t$ days is given by the function\n\n$$\nS(t)=40+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in days, since the conference was announced. \n\nAt what time is the number of participants at a minimum, and how many participants are registered at this time?" :question/worked-solution "To find when the number participants is minimized, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(40+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(40)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4t-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0$:\n\n$$\n4x-16=0\\,⟹\\,t=4\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=4.$ To find out how many participants are registered when $t=4,$ we figure out $S(4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(4) & =40+{\\int }_{0}^{4}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =40+{[2{x}^{2}-16x]|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =40+[(2(4)^{2}-16(4))-(0)] \\\\  & =40-32 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $8<40$, we conclude that the minimum number of participants is $8$, and this occurs after $4$ days."}]}
